From 0ecf46d0a2cc7ea21a956a35d5ef7219614112c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:52:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] l5-pmus-live: read-only diagnostic for the rows venue
 cost attestation gave up on

For each settled row still at the assumed $1.00 bound that the attestation
exhausted its attempts on, log the ledger's quantities and cost beside the
venue's fill-derived quantities, cost and fees, the difference, which
reconciliation form (if any) would have matched, and whether the row settled
before the last accounting re-anchor. Also a summary of corrections posted
after a re-anchor for rows that settled before it.

Reads store.state and the activity feed (GET). Calls no store method, saves
nothing, keeps progress in memory, feeds no gate. Off unless
L5_VENUE_COST_DIAGNOSTIC is exactly READ_ONLY. Hook in the runner is gated
and swallows every exception.

31 tests. Not deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HTk927uH8zwpj6gLES92PF
